  data:  # 7885
    kind: work_item  # 7885
    title: "swift: var_types pools EVERY type's stored properties with true globals in one name-keyed file map, consulted BEFORE the enclosing type's own fields -- type A's property types a same-named receiver in type B"  # 7885
    status: todo_hard  # 7885
    priority: 3  # 7885
    parent:  # 7885
    tags:  # 7885
    - swift  # 7885
    - analysis_quality  # 7885
    isbefore: []  # 7885
    duplicate_of: []  # 7885
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7885
    pr_ref:  # 7885
    description: "FILED 2026-10-04 from WI-silos-mufon-mular-gavik-hihip-mibuj-mihov-julim (branch jgstern-agent/fix/silos).\n\nMECHANISM. swift.py `_extract_edges_from_file` keeps ONE name-keyed map, `var_types`, for every FILE-LEVEL declaration: top-level globals AND the stored properties of EVERY type declared in the file (a property's scope chain stops at its class_declaration, so it lands at file level). `_type_of` consults `var_types` BEFORE `_inherited_field_type` (the enclosing type's own fields, through its bases), and writes are last-writer-wins. So:\n  (a) a property of type A types a same-named bare receiver inside type B, which has no such member;\n  (b) when a global and a property share a name, whichever is declared LATER in the file wins, in every type.\n\nLIVE REPRO (origin/dev 385ec63be1, analyze_swift on a one-file fixture):\n  class A { var store: FileManager = FileManager.default }\n  class B { func go() { store.zap() } }\n  -> swift:FileManager:0-0:zap:unresolved, receiver_type_hint FileManager (B has no `store`).\n\nCORPUS INSTANCES (read back while measuring WI-silos):\n  Kingfisher Sources/Cache/DiskStorage.swift:122/250/397 `let fileManager = config.fileManager` -- before WI-silos the local was untyped and `fileManager.fileExists` etc. were typed FileManager from the nested `Config` struct's `fileManager` property via var_types (right by coincidence; Backend has no such member). These are 3 catalogued fs chains (fs_read FileManager.enumerator, fs_read FileManager.fileExists, fs_write FileManager.createDirectory).\n  hummingbird Sources/Hummingbird/Application.swift:99-117 `let responder = try await self.responder` in a protocol extension -- typed Responder from `struct Application`'s `public let responder: Responder` (line 190) in the same file.\n\nWI-silos deliberately left the file level typed-only and position-free (a tombstone in a map shared by every type would hide same-named fields of all the others). The structural fix is to stop pooling type members with globals: a type's properties belong to that type (the field-type registry already holds them by owner), and only true globals belong to the file level, looked up AFTER the enclosing type's members (Swift's unqualified lookup order: locals, then members of the enclosing type, then module scope)."  # 7885
    fields: {}  # 7885
- op: discuss  # f9b0
  at: '2026-10-05T00:29:04Z'  # f9b0
  by: agent  # f9b0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f9b0
  clock: 2  # f9b0
  nonce: f9b0  # f9b0
  message: "Worked on branch jgstern-agent/fix/hojib (with WI-hojib, on top of WI-silos 41fd9834a6). Commits 952164dd8c, ef734925a8, eabbd346cd. Not pushed.\n\nA file-level declaration is now a MEMBER of its owning type, recorded by declaration span and by owner name, or a true global in var_types. A bare name resolves: innermost local -> the enclosing declaration's own members -> the type's members through bases (file members, then the field registry) -> globals. In addition:\n- same-named nested types keep their own members (Alamofire Combine.swift `Inner` x3);\n- `extension A.B` finds B's members;\n- a protocol's property requirement is a member of the protocol and its conformers;\n- a generic parameter or `associatedtype` is not a member type;\n- Pass 1 no longer registers init / closure / accessor locals as fields.\n\nLive repro (the filed fixture):\n- origin/dev: `swift:FileManager:0-0:zap`, hint FileManager.\n- branch: `swift:external:0-0:zap:unresolved`, hint None.\n- control inside A: FileManager.\n\nTests: test_swift_member_scope.py was red on the silos tree, is green now, and was mutation-checked. Corpus read-back: last-writer stamps from the pooled map are replaced by each declaration's own:\n- URLEncoding x32 in URLParameterEncodingTestCase;\n- `request` per publisher;\n- `container` Map x18;\n- `lock` UnfairLock.\n\nhummingbird Application.swift:117 (`responder` in the protocol extension) is now untyped. The protocol's `responder` has type `associatedtype Responder`, a type parameter. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/hojib.md."  # f9b0
