  by: agent  # 3aa4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3aa4
  clock: 4  # 3aa4
  nonce: 3aa4  # 3aa4
  message: "Merged in PR #1459 (dev ecbb226a0d).\n\nFixed in PR #1459 (commits 952164dd8c, ef734925a8, eabbd346cd).\n\nA type's properties are recorded under their owning declaration and type name, and only true globals stay in var_types. A bare name resolves locals, then the enclosing type's own members (through its bases), then globals.\n\nBehavioral evidence: the item's live repro, `class A { var store: FileManager }` / `class B { func go() { store.zap() } }`:\n- origin/dev: `swift:FileManager:0-0:zap`, hint FileManager.\n- branch: `swift:external:0-0:zap:unresolved`, hint None.\n- Control `store.zip()` inside A: FileManager.\n\ntest_swift_member_scope.py was red on the silos tree, is green on the branch, and is mutation-checked (members pooled into globals -> 4 red; globals before members -> 2 red). It covers:\n- global vs member in either declaration order;\n- an untyped member shadowing a global;\n- same-named nested `Inner` types (Alamofire Combine.swift);\n- `extension A.B`;\n- protocol requirements;\n- associatedtypes;\n- init-locals that are no longer fields.\n\nCorpus instances:\n- Kingfisher `config.fileManager` is now typed through Config's own member, not through the pooled map. The 3 catalogued chains return, as above.\n- hummingbird Application.swift:117 `responder` in the protocol extension is now untyped. The protocol's `responder` has type `associatedtype Responder`, a type parameter, not a type.\n\nRead-back of the changed classes: the pooled map's last-writer stamps are replaced by each declaration's own:\n- `encoding` URLEncoding ×32;\n- `request` per publisher;\n- `container` Map ×18;\n- `lock` UnfairLock;\n- `encoder` JSONEncoder.\n\nNOT asserted: same-named nested types REFERENCED by name from outside their declaration still share one name-keyed entry (first writer)."  # 3aa4
